# Walkthrough: Stance System & THREAT vs WILL AI

## Summary
Implemented the full 12-point Stance Equilibrium Scale and wired THREAT vs WILL into the AI decision-making pipeline.

---

## 1. The 12-Point Stance Scale — [HumanoidCore.gd](file:///c:/Users/Zerato/OneDrive/Documents/arccross_system/BiologicalCore/HumanoidCore.gd)

New variables:
- `stance_points: int = 12` — the raw equilibrium value
- `current_stance: GameEnums.StanceState` — derived bracket

New signals:
- `stance_changed(new_state, points)` — fires on any state transition
- `felled()` — fires specifically when hitting 0, for UI/combat hooks

### State Brackets
| Points | State | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| 7–12 | `PLANTED` | Full action set. Normal THREAT projection. |
| 1–6 | `STUMBLING` | Restricted actions. Cannot flee. THREAT drops to **0**. |
| 0 | `FELLED` | Stunned for one round. Open to `EXECUTE`. |

### Methods
- `apply_stance_damage(amount)` — Called by CombatResolutionEngine after armor resolution. Returns the resulting StanceState.
- `recover_stance(amount)` — Natural recovery per round (you can hook this into the turn cycle).
- `reset_stance()` — Full reset after a successful `GET_UP` action.
- `get_effective_threat()` — Returns 0 if STUMBLING/FELLED, otherwise returns gear THREAT. This is what the AI reads.

---

## 2. Combat Integration — [CombatResolutionEngine.gd](file:///c:/Users/Zerato/OneDrive/Documents/arccross_system/CombatCore/CombatResolutionEngine.gd)

The stance damage TODO has been replaced with a live call:
- `victim.apply_stance_damage(final_stance)` is called after armor resolution.
- BLUNT weapons bypass armor for stance damage — they crush equilibrium even through plate armor.
- SHARP/BALLISTIC stance damage is reduced by armor.

---

## 3. THREAT vs WILL AI — [CombatAIEvaluator.gd](file:///c:/Users/Zerato/OneDrive/Documents/arccross_system/CombatCore/CombatAIEvaluator.gd)

### On Turn Start
The very first thing the AI does when its turn begins is size up the player:
1. Reads `target_core.get_effective_threat()` (which returns 0 if the player is STUMBLING)
2. Passes it to `_evaluate_flight_response(player_threat)`
3. If `THREAT > WILL` and the AI is `SURVIVALIST`, it **immediately flees** before even scoring tactics.

### New Scoring: `_score_execute()`
- Returns **15.0** (the highest score in the game) if the target is `FELLED` and in the same grid.
- The AI will always prioritize finishing off a downed opponent over everything else.

### Stance-Aware Retreat
- `STUMBLING` AI entities now score retreat at 0.7 even if not fleeing — they instinctively try to create distance when off-balance.

